{"name":"Mad Scientist","title":"Mad Scientist","revision":231789,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Mad_Scientist","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The primary visuals associated with mad scientists are their laboratories, which feature a simultaneously ominous and campy atmosphere. Technologies in the lab are designed to look confusing, imposing, and cartoonish. The results of their experiments are also a frequent and reliable visual aspect. Neon green is the color most commonly associated with mad scientists."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Note, because the list of Mad Scientist characters is extensive, please include media where the mad scientist is central to the narrative and has the aesthetic."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus (1818)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Girl Genius (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde (1886)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Franny K. Stein series (2004-2022)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Western Animation"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dexter's Laboratory (1996)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pinky and the Brain (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mad Scientist (1988)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Monster Lab (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Invader Zim (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Adventures of Jimmy Neutron (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Phineas and Ferb (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Futurama (1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rick and Morty (2013)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Live-Action TV"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Munsters (1964)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mystery Science Theatre 3000 (1988)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maniac Mansion (1990)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maniac Mansion (1987)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dr. Muto (2002)"},{"kind":